 "PN-Q197": "<article class=\"qi need\" data-id=\"PN-Q197\" data-plan=\"PN\" data-tier=\"need\" data-rec=\"A\"><div class=\"qt\">You said numbers should follow date order automatically. Which way?</div><div class=\"why\"><b>Your note:</b> “they should auto update to the chronological order.” <b>Why it matters:</b> This replaces “each person keeps their own numbers” (PN-Q1, which you agreed earlier). With A nobody ever types a version number, so a clash can't happen and Leo and Mikey have nothing new to learn. Old links keep working: each old number stays as a hidden alias.</div><div class=\"ops abc\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ob\" data-a=\"A\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><b>A</b><span>One shared list, numbered automatically by the date each note goes live (v0.1, v0.2 … for everyone, with a Harry / Leo / Mikey badge). All 65 old notes are renumbered by date once.</span><span class=\"rk\">Recommended</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ob\" data-a=\"B\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><b>B</b><span>Each person keeps their own numbers (as planned), but the archive always lists every note in date order.</span></button></div><div class=\"qf\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"nb\" data-a=\"note\" aria-pressed=\"false\">✎ Note</button><span class=\"was\" hidden></span><span class=\"qid\">PN-Q197</span></div><input class=\"qn\" type=\"text\" maxlength=\"300\" placeholder=\"One-line note\" aria-label=\"Note for PN-Q197\" hidden></article>"
